# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The private side folder. Everything under it stays local: material extracted
# from the game, files derived from its source, and the reverse-engineering and
# decompilation notes.
#
# This is the single most important line in the repo. The .githooks/pre-commit
# hook refuses any staged path under _local/ as well, so a stray `git add -f`
# cannot get past both.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/_local/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Defence in depth: even outside _local/, never track the game, anything
# extracted from it, or anything generated from its source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The game itself, in any form
*.exe
*.gmk
*.gm6
*.gb1
*.dll
battleshipsforeverv090d*/
bsf-*/
wineprefix/

# Extracted / decompiled game data
objects.json
scripts.json
dump/
mem_ships/
gallery/
*.shp
*.sb4

# Files GENERATED from the game's own GML -- these are derivative works and must
# be rebuilt by each user from their own copy, never redistributed.
mods/crisp_widgets.gml
mods/x3patch.gml
mods/x3_*.gml
mods/stepprof.gml
mods/turretprof.gml
mods/turret_step.gml
mods/eturret_step.gml

# Runtime state written by the mods next to themselves
mods/*.on
mods/*.log
mods/*.txt
mods/*.cfg
mods/*.png
mods/*.req

# ...except the markers that decide which modules are ON. These are empty files
# and they ARE the default configuration: without them a fresh clone installs
# every module and enables none of them. battle.on is deliberately absent -- it
# is a scripted stress battle for measurement, not something a player wants.
!mods/cursor.on
!mods/crisp.on
!mods/logo.on
!mods/legacy.on

# Build + scratch
tmp/
build/
toolchain/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-machine git hooks, and the root symlink to the local half of CLAUDE.md
# (the file itself lives under _local/, which is already excluded above).
/.githooks/
/CLAUDE.local.md

# Claude Code config. The skills and slash commands ARE part of this repo, but
# they are named one at a time rather than re-included wholesale. Everything
# else that lands under .claude/ -- a personal command, a skill belonging to
# other work, a scratch note, the worktrees managed here -- then stays out by
# default rather than arriving in the next `git add -A`. Adding a skill costs
# one line here, and forgetting it means the skill is missing (which you notice)
# instead of something private being published (which you might not).
#
# Each directory has to be un-excluded by name for two reasons: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, and the bsf-*/ rule
# above -- meant for scratch copies of the game dir -- matches every skill
# folder as well.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/commands/
/.claude/commands/*
!/.claude/commands/git_branch_status.md
!/.claude/commands/git_commit_merge_wt.md
!/.claude/skills/
/.claude/skills/*
!/.claude/skills/bsf-ships/
!/.claude/skills/bsf-capture/
!/.claude/skills/bsf-storytelling/

# ...but NOT the campaign reference that skill generates. CAMPAIGN.html is the
# game's own briefings and comm traffic, extracted verbatim by
# bsf-storytelling/scripts/extract-campaign.py -- exactly the thing this repo
# never publishes. Ship the generator, never its output. This rule comes after
# the re-include above because the last matching pattern wins.
/.claude/skills/bsf-storytelling/CAMPAIGN.html
